        "date": "2026-11-12T05:47:41Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(import): mirror ruststep's tokenizer in the STEP nesting scan\n\nReview of PR #1079: a `<...>` REFERENCE resource or ANCHOR name holding\n`/*` or `'` put the depth scan into a comment or string state ruststep\nnever entered, so a 5000-deep record after it passed the check and\noverflowed the stack. The scan gains a `<...>` state and a binary `\"...\"`\nstate (parentheses still counted there), after an end-to-end read of\nruststep's tokenizer at the pinned rev; the construct table lives in the\nmodule and the decision file, and the Cargo.toml pin comment says the scan\nmust be re-audited when the pin moves. Table-driven tests pin every\nconstruct at the cap + 1.\n\nFixes #1075\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
